THIRD-PARTY LICENSES AND ATTRIBUTIONS
================================================================================

This benchmark includes test cases derived from the following third-party 
sources. Each retains its original license as specified below:

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Garak Framework
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

License: Apache License 2.0
Test Cases: 51 cases (9.8% of benchmark)
Original Work: https://github.com/leondz/garak
Authors: Leon Derczynski et al.

Attribution: "Based on Garak by Leon Derczynski et al. 
              (https://github.com/leondz/garak)"

These test cases are inspired by attack patterns and examples from the Garak
framework, adapted and modified for inclusion in PIDB.

Full Apache 2.0 License: https://github.com/leondz/garak/blob/main/LICENSE

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. NotInject Dataset
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0)
Test Cases: 339 cases (64.8% of benchmark)

Attribution: "Derived from NotInject dataset"

These test cases focus on preventing false positives in guardrail systems.
They have been adapted to fit PIDB's schema and standardized format.

Full CC-BY-4.0 License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Original PIDB Test Cases
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

License: MIT (same as repository)
Test Cases: 133 cases (25.4% of benchmark)
Creator: Directive Commons and contributors

These are original test cases created specifically for PIDB, including
advanced encoding attacks, multilingual attacks, ultra-sophisticated attacks,
and LLM-specific attacks. These are covered by the MIT License above.

